Facts from other projects
-------------------------

The protocol facts come from public descriptions, chiefly python-kasa
(github.com/python-kasa/python-kasa, GPL-3.0), through the tplink module.
Since v0.2.0 the Tapo energy history fields also come from
fabiankachlock/tapo-api (MIT) and mihai-dinculescu/tapo (MIT). No code,
effect table or default credential was taken from any of them. The Kasa
camera simulator can take any login (AnyLogin) so that clients with a
built-in default can be tested; it holds no such default itself.

Interop tests (interop/, a separate test-only module)
-----------------------------------------------------

interop/peer/Dockerfile installs python-kasa 0.11.0.1 (GPL-3.0) from
PyPI into a python:3.12.10-slim image at test time; nothing of
python-kasa is copied into this repository, and it is not linked with
this module. interop/peer/client.py is our own script that calls
python-kasa.

Since v0.3.0, interop/tapopeer/Dockerfile installs the Python bindings of
mihai-dinculescu/tapo 0.11.1 (MIT) from PyPI into a second image at test
time; interop/tapopeer/schedule.py is our own script that calls it.
Nothing of it is copied into this repository. The camera and robot
vacuum requests the simulators answer follow the same facts as the tplink
module (python-kasa, pytapo (MIT) and the tapo crate; facts only).

